{# The mail service connection on the Delivery page: its address and state, the From address's sending domain,
   and Connect, Disconnect and Forget (Admin\DeliveryConnectionController), which only administrators see. #}
<div class="card{{ configured ? '' : ' border-warning' }}">
  <div class="card-header fw-semibold d-flex flex-row flex-wrap justify-content-between align-items-center gap-3">
    <span>Mail service</span>
    {% if uses_connection %}<span class="badge theme-success">Connected</span>
    {% elseif configured %}<span class="badge theme-secondary">Configured in .env</span>
    {% else %}<span class="badge theme-warning">Not connected</span>{% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="card-body small">
    {% if address %}
      <p class="mb-3">Address: {% include 'layout/_copy.html.twig' with {value: address, id: 'mail-service-address', label: 'the mail service\'s address'} %}
        <span class="fg-2">{{ address_source == 'env' ? '(from .env)' : (address_source == 'settings' ? '(set on the Settings page)' : '') }}</span></p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if uses_connection and connection %}
      <p class="mb-1">Connected{% if connection.client_name %} with the account <strong>{{ connection.client_name }}</strong>{% endif %}{% if connection.application_name %}, under the name “{{ connection.application_name }}”{% endif %}.</p>
      <p class="fg-2">{% if connection.connected_at %}Since {{ connection.connected_at|slice(0, 16) }}{% if connection.connected_by %}, by {{ connection.connected_by }}{% endif %}. {% endif %}The key and the webhook secret came from the mail service and are stored encrypted; they are never shown.</p>
    {% elseif configured %}
      <p>The mail service is set in this installation's .env ({{ env_settings|join(', ') }}). A value in .env takes precedence over a connection made here.</p>
      {% if connection %}<div class="alert theme-warning" role="note"><i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle" aria-hidden="true"></i><div>A connection to {{ connection.service }} is stored here as well, but .env takes precedence over it. Remove the settings from .env to use it, or disconnect it.</div></div>{% endif %}
    {% elseif connection_problem %}
      <div class="alert theme-danger" role="alert"><i class="bi bi-exclamation-octagon" aria-hidden="true"></i><div>A connection{% if connection %} to {{ connection.service }}{% endif %} is stored, but its key cannot be read: {{ connection_problem }} Restore the APP_SETTINGS_KEY it was saved with, or connect again.</div></div>
    {% else %}
      <p>No mail service is connected, so campaign mail cannot be sent yet. {% if is_administrator %}<a href="{{ path('admin_sending_setup') }}">Set up sending</a> takes you through it step by step: the mail service account, Connect, the sending domain and a test message.{% else %}An administrator sets it up under Settings › Set up sending.{% endif %}</p>
    {% endif %}

    {% if configured %}
      {% if from_domain.state == 'ok' %}
        <p class="mb-0"><i class="bi bi-check-circle fg-success me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>Mail from <strong>{{ from_domain.domain }}</strong> (the site's From address) can be sent. <span class="fg-2">Checked {{ from_domain.checked_at|slice(0, 16) }}.</span></p>
      {% elseif from_domain.state == 'cannot_send' %}
        <div class="alert theme-warning mb-0" role="alert"><i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle" aria-hidden="true"></i><div><strong>Mail from {{ from_domain.domain }} cannot be sent yet.</strong> The domain of the site's From address is in your account at the mail service, but its DNS records are not all published yet. {% if domain_steps %}<a href="{{ domain_steps }}">Open its DNS steps</a> at the mail service: they show each record with a copy button and check it by themselves.{% else %}Finish its setup in your account at the mail service.{% endif %} <span class="fg-2">Checked {{ from_domain.checked_at|slice(0, 16) }}.</span></div></div>
      {% elseif from_domain.state == 'not_registered' %}
        <div class="alert theme-warning mb-0" role="alert"><i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle" aria-hidden="true"></i><div><strong>Mail from {{ from_domain.domain }} cannot be sent.</strong> The domain of the site's From address is not a sending domain of your account at the mail service. Add it there (Settings › Sending domains), or change this site's From address (Settings › Sender); then use <strong>Check connection</strong>. <span class="fg-2">Checked {{ from_domain.checked_at|slice(0, 16) }}.</span></div></div>
      {% elseif from_domain.state == 'no_from_address' %}
        <div class="alert theme-warning mb-0" role="note"><i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle" aria-hidden="true"></i><div>The site has no From address (Settings › Sender), so whether its domain can send is not known.</div></div>
      {% else %}
        <p class="mb-0 fg-2">Whether mail from {{ from_domain.domain }} (the site's From address) can be sent has not been checked yet: use <strong>Check connection</strong>.</p>
      {% endif %}
      {% if waiting_for_domain ?? false %}
        <p class="mt-3 mb-0 fg-2"><i class="bi bi-arrow-repeat me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>While the domain is being set up at the mail service, the worker asks it again every minute and this page updates itself.</p>
      {% endif %}
      {% if not sending_setup_done and is_administrator %}
        <p class="mt-3 mb-0"><a href="{{ path('admin_sending_setup') }}"><i class="bi bi-list-check me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>Set up sending</a> <span class="fg-2">shows what is left to do.</span></p>
      {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% if is_administrator %}
    <div class="card-footer small">
      {% if connect_obstacle and not connection %}
        <p class="mb-0 fg-2">{{ connect_obstacle }}</p>
      {% else %}
        {% if connect_obstacle %}<p class="fg-2">{{ connect_obstacle }}</p>{% endif %}
        {% if connect_form %}
          {% include 'admin/_delivery_connect_form.html.twig' with {form: connect_form, obstacle: connect_obstacle, label: connection ? 'Connect again' : 'Connect'} %}
        {% endif %}
        {% if connection %}
          <form class="d-flex flex-row flex-wrap align-items-center gap-3 mt-5 pt-5 border-top" method="post" action="{{ path('admin_delivery_disconnect') }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{ csrf_token('ctnlist') }}">
            <button class="btn-solid theme-danger" type="submit" data-confirm="Disconnect the mail service? It revokes this site's key and removes its webhook endpoint; campaign mail cannot be sent until a mail service is connected again."><i class="bi bi-plug me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>Disconnect</button>
            <button class="btn-outline theme-secondary" type="submit" name="forget" value="1" data-confirm="Forget the stored connection without telling the mail service? Its key stays valid there until the connection is ended in your account there.">Forget without revoking</button>
            <span class="fg-2">Disconnect ends the connection at the mail service, then clears what is stored here; the address is kept. Forget only clears what is stored here, for a mail service that no longer answers.</span>
          </form>
        {% endif %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {% elseif not configured %}
    <div class="card-footer small"><p class="mb-0 fg-2">An administrator can connect the mail service here.</p></div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
